WEBVTT

00:04.860 --> 00:07.380
And tonight, I will be servicing...

00:07.380 --> 00:11.790
a 28 year old office worker,

00:11.790 --> 00:14.530
who is currently worried about getting married to a man without a steady job.

00:16.460 --> 00:18.410
I see.

00:18.410 --> 00:22.570
Though I have to say marriage counseling is hardly the job of a host.

00:22.570 --> 00:24.690
To put this into "shopping" terms,

00:24.690 --> 00:26.910
have you ever once truly felt satisfied

00:26.910 --> 00:30.520
after you've bought something that you've spent hours debating on whether you should buy or not?

00:30.520 --> 00:31.910
I...

00:31.910 --> 00:34.650
Money should only be spent on

00:34.650 --> 00:38.610
those things that are truly worthwhile.

00:39.760 --> 00:41.420
Reiji...

00:41.420 --> 00:43.580
That being said,

00:43.580 --> 00:46.910
why not consider buying me?

00:47.670 --> 00:49.960
For a limited one time offer,

00:49.960 --> 00:54.410
with immediate purchase, I come included with peace of mind for you.

00:55.390 --> 00:56.270
You're so cute!

00:56.270 --> 00:57.250
Can I touch those?

00:57.250 --> 00:58.780
Your ears are so plushy!

00:59.880 --> 01:01.140
Don't hate.

01:01.140 --> 01:03.280
I'm only doing my job.

01:03.280 --> 01:05.220
Here's the champagne tower you ordered.

01:05.520 --> 01:07.820
Thank you for your patronage!

02:38.310 --> 02:39.570
Let's go!

02:39.570 --> 02:41.410
Animal Soldiers.

02:45.550 --> 02:46.330
Usakotsu!

02:46.330 --> 02:47.500
The Animal Soldiers are

02:47.500 --> 02:48.270
Devilcat!

02:48.270 --> 02:50.030
a horrific group of killers

02:50.860 --> 02:53.450
in stuffed animal monster form,

02:53.450 --> 02:54.520
They're so cute!

02:54.520 --> 02:58.660
affiliated with the evil organization known as Florsheim.

02:58.660 --> 03:00.420
Let me go already!

03:03.310 --> 03:04.270
Let's go!

03:04.270 --> 03:06.160
Animal Soldiers.

03:09.060 --> 03:12.210
Let's come up with a plan to get rid of Red by ourselves.

03:12.210 --> 03:13.050
Yeah.

03:13.050 --> 03:15.080
How about we get him from behind with a huge cauldron?

03:15.080 --> 03:17.680
Isn't that a little too predictable?

03:17.680 --> 03:19.070
I guess it is.

03:20.290 --> 03:22.230
This is hard.

03:32.660 --> 03:33.770
Let's go!

03:33.770 --> 03:35.510
Animal Soldiers.

03:38.690 --> 03:41.660
P-chan Custom is a customization freak,

03:41.660 --> 03:44.890
and loves it to the point where he can't stop modifying himself.

03:50.960 --> 03:54.300
Where are you trying to go, P-chan?

03:57.460 --> 03:59.830
General Vamp's Quick Recipes.

03:59.830 --> 04:02.190
How's it going guys, Vamp here.

04:02.190 --> 04:05.840
You're watching the fourth episode of our beloved series.

04:05.840 --> 04:08.300
Let's cook our hats off today!

04:08.500 --> 04:11.980
We'll be cooking a very simple dish as usual today:

04:11.980 --> 04:13.240
A tomato toast.

04:13.640 --> 04:15.230
The ingredients you'll need are:

04:15.230 --> 04:16.350
a slice of bread,

04:16.350 --> 04:17.630
some mayonnaise,

04:17.630 --> 04:19.100
a tomato,

04:19.100 --> 04:20.400
and that's about it.

04:20.400 --> 04:22.020
Getting right to the cooking,

04:22.020 --> 04:25.280
you need to first toast the bread,

04:25.280 --> 04:28.220
and have the tomato sliced while the bread's in the toaster.

04:28.220 --> 04:29.890
Slice it to any size you like;

04:29.890 --> 04:33.670
thick or thin, it shouldn't matter.

04:33.860 --> 04:35.690
Is the bread toasted yet?

04:35.690 --> 04:39.450
Take the toasted bread, and spread mayonnaise over it.

04:39.450 --> 04:41.070
Again, the amount of mayo to spread is totally up to you.

04:41.070 --> 04:45.020
Place the tomato slices on top of the mayo'd bread and...

04:45.980 --> 04:47.330
Voila.

04:47.330 --> 04:49.850
A very simple tomato toast is ready.

04:49.850 --> 04:52.590
I'm sure you've all thought about making this at least once.

04:52.590 --> 04:55.500
Mayonnaise spreads easier on bread than butter does,

04:55.500 --> 04:57.320
so it's perfect for those lazy cooks who live alone.

04:57.320 --> 04:59.850
Toasty, toasty!

04:59.850 --> 05:01.630
Come on now, Tiser.

05:01.630 --> 05:03.890
You're getting bread crumbs everywhere.

05:09.550 --> 05:10.630
Master Vamp!

05:10.630 --> 05:11.570
Did you really get one?

05:11.570 --> 05:12.930
I want to see!

05:12.930 --> 05:15.190
Hold your horses.

05:15.490 --> 05:17.130
Tada!

05:18.000 --> 05:20.350
It's the Rakutin model designed for the elderly.

05:20.350 --> 05:22.780
I had Geirus set up the ringtone for me.

05:22.780 --> 05:25.520
Let's see now, hang on...

05:25.520 --> 05:26.170
And there.

05:26.170 --> 05:28.210
This song's pretty popular, isn't it?

05:33.870 --> 05:35.710
Shuuchishin?

05:39.480 --> 05:41.640
Hello, is this Kayoko?

05:41.640 --> 05:44.270
Vamp? What's going on?

05:44.550 --> 05:47.110
I just bought a phone, so I figured I'd test it out.

05:47.500 --> 05:48.980
So you finally got one.

05:48.980 --> 05:50.260
Yup, yup.

05:50.260 --> 05:53.830
I did have my reservations, but I guess it really is convenient to have one.

05:53.830 --> 05:57.020
Oh yeah, I've been meaning to ask you something, Vamp.

05:58.240 --> 06:00.140
How to make oden soup?

06:01.030 --> 06:02.760
Don't put a lid on the pot when you're boiling the soup,

06:02.760 --> 06:05.890
or else the oden's going to get all bloated and the soup's going to get cloudy.

06:05.890 --> 06:08.560
Oh and the flavor actually settles in when you're cooling the soup.

06:08.560 --> 06:10.920
Yeah, you shouldn't boil it for too long.

06:10.920 --> 06:12.980
Yup, you should keep alternating the heat on and off.

06:12.980 --> 06:14.070
Sure.

06:14.070 --> 06:17.270
Feel free to call me if you have any more questions, okay?

06:17.270 --> 06:19.830
Okay, bye.

06:19.830 --> 06:20.970
Master Vamp,

06:20.970 --> 06:23.270
what should we have for dinner tonight?

06:24.250 --> 06:25.590
Master Vamp?

06:25.590 --> 06:27.910
I wonder if she understood everything over the phone.

06:29.140 --> 06:31.260
Actually, I'm worried. I'm going to go see if everything's okay.

06:31.260 --> 06:32.310
Where are you off to?

06:32.310 --> 06:32.910
Oden soup!

06:32.910 --> 06:34.330
Gobou roll, Gobou roll.

06:34.330 --> 06:35.940
I take it we're having oden soup for dinner then?

06:35.940 --> 06:37.620
Chikuwabu.

06:39.870 --> 06:41.530
You came all the way here to check on me?

06:41.530 --> 06:42.470
Yeah.

06:42.470 --> 06:45.310
Thanks for the concern, but I'm afraid you'll have to go back right away.

06:46.040 --> 06:48.250
We're actually having guests over, right now.

06:48.900 --> 06:50.110
<i>His</i> friends will be here.

06:51.110 --> 06:52.450
His friends?

06:52.820 --> 06:54.330
They're heroes.

06:54.330 --> 06:55.410
And there's two of 'em.

06:55.410 --> 06:57.420
I was cooking the oden soup for <i>them</i>.

06:57.840 --> 07:00.300
Then I guess it would be best for me to be on my way.

07:01.950 --> 07:02.900
Oh crap, they're here!

07:02.900 --> 07:04.180
You have to hide, Vamp!

07:05.030 --> 07:06.930
The closet in the tatami room is empty, so hurry!

07:06.930 --> 07:08.300
Right, right.

07:09.430 --> 07:10.650
Welcome to our home!

07:11.720 --> 07:12.480
It's me.

07:12.980 --> 07:14.700
What about your friends?

07:14.700 --> 07:16.280
I waited for them over at the train station,

07:16.280 --> 07:19.660
but they didn't come, so I thought maybe they came here instead.

07:20.700 --> 07:21.530
Oh yeah.

07:21.530 --> 07:23.100
Vamp is here.

07:24.700 --> 07:26.120
Hi, how's it going.

07:26.120 --> 07:28.200
What the hell are you doing in our closet?

07:28.200 --> 07:31.210
I told him to hide because I thought your friends were here.

07:31.210 --> 07:32.890
What the hell are you doing here?

07:33.710 --> 07:35.800
I was concerned about your oden soup, and-

07:35.800 --> 07:36.960
That's none of your concern!

07:38.010 --> 07:40.070
Oh, the phone's ringing. Please excuse me for one second.

07:40.470 --> 07:42.040
Hello?

07:42.840 --> 07:44.020
Ueda?

07:44.320 --> 07:46.020
You've got the wrong number.

07:46.020 --> 07:49.050
This is Vamp of Florsheim speaking.

07:49.650 --> 07:51.340
No, not at all.

07:51.660 --> 07:53.190
He had the wrong number.

07:53.190 --> 07:55.440
Why do you have Shuuchishin as your ringtone?

07:55.440 --> 07:57.640
Never mind, just go home.

07:57.640 --> 07:59.110
Go before my friends get here.

07:59.110 --> 07:59.780
Sure.

07:59.780 --> 08:01.350
I shouldn't be saying this,

08:01.350 --> 08:03.780
but you don't want to mess with these guys.

08:03.780 --> 08:06.660
Well then, thanks for having me over, Kayoko.

08:06.660 --> 08:09.250
My pleasure. Feel free to come back anytime.

08:09.250 --> 08:09.870
I will.

08:09.870 --> 08:11.090
You most definitely will not!

08:11.490 --> 08:12.460
Holy shit, they're here!

08:12.460 --> 08:14.990
Go hide in the closet again!

08:14.990 --> 08:18.090
We're coming in, Red.

08:21.200 --> 08:24.490
Long time no see, Fraternal Warriors Abasilin.

08:24.490 --> 08:25.490
W-Welcome!

08:26.190 --> 08:28.200
It's been a while, Red.

08:28.200 --> 08:29.550
I-Indeed.

08:29.550 --> 08:31.450
I see you're as huge as ever.

08:31.450 --> 08:35.510
And you've become a fine woman since I last saw you, Kayoko.

08:35.510 --> 08:36.890
Let me guess,

08:36.890 --> 08:41.740
you and Red have been getting on some XXX action every night, haven't you?

08:42.200 --> 08:44.830
Oh stop, Abasilver.

08:44.830 --> 08:46.060
XXX he said.

08:47.530 --> 08:50.350
Do you drink whiskey, Abagold?

08:50.350 --> 08:52.120
What are you saying, Mineko.

08:52.120 --> 08:52.930
Mineko?

08:52.930 --> 08:54.190
I'll drink anything.

08:54.190 --> 08:57.240
You can stop serving now Kayoko. Come sit down.

08:57.240 --> 08:59.160
Really? Okay then.

08:59.160 --> 09:00.980
Kayoko!

09:00.980 --> 09:04.970
You don't have to be all polite and everything.

09:05.320 --> 09:08.030
So what brings you guys here from Hokkaido today?

09:08.030 --> 09:09.490
Oh yeah.

09:09.490 --> 09:12.680
We wanted to hunt some monsters in Tokyo.

09:12.680 --> 09:15.290
But damn it, we haven't found any worthwhile ones yet!

09:15.290 --> 09:16.850
It's actually kinda like <i>that</i>.

09:16.850 --> 09:18.330
Monsters from the city are kinda like <i>that</i>.

09:18.330 --> 09:19.730
Yeah they're really all like <i>that</i>.

09:19.730 --> 09:21.640
They're all earnest or serious or something.

09:21.640 --> 09:22.650
Yeah.

09:22.650 --> 09:25.790
We already showed all the monsters up in Hokkaido who's boss.

09:25.790 --> 09:27.460
I wanna kick some ass!

09:27.460 --> 09:30.330
My blood's boiling for some more hero action!

09:30.730 --> 09:35.060
Didn't Hokkaido used to be infested with those monsters from the "Death Bruins?"

09:35.060 --> 09:36.920
They've <i>been</i> history.

09:36.920 --> 09:39.260
This fool got drunk,

09:39.260 --> 09:42.630
and attacked the Death Bruins while they were sleeping.

09:42.990 --> 09:45.010
But you were the one who came from behind,

09:45.010 --> 09:46.430
I mean, you came later on,

09:46.430 --> 09:48.560
and really fucked them, really really fucked them up!

09:48.560 --> 09:51.150
They were all fucked up from the front and the back.

09:51.830 --> 09:53.590
These guys really are something.

09:54.640 --> 09:58.020
The monsters around here really have no power at all.

09:58.020 --> 10:00.250
That's power with a capital "P."

10:00.750 --> 10:03.170
Where am I supposed to bring justice to now?

10:03.170 --> 10:04.270
What should I do?

10:04.270 --> 10:07.650
If they find me here, I'm done for!

10:10.430 --> 10:11.750
Did I hear something?

10:11.750 --> 10:13.490
That dumbass!

10:13.490 --> 10:15.240
You must be hearing things.

10:15.240 --> 10:17.620
No, dumbass, I hear it loud and clear.

10:17.620 --> 10:19.890
Yeah, it's definitely Shuuchishin.

10:20.430 --> 10:21.550
Oh my god.

10:21.550 --> 10:23.220
How do I turn this off?

10:23.220 --> 10:25.820
I haven't even had time to figure out this phone yet!

10:26.120 --> 10:27.900
So you're into Shuuchishin these days, huh?

10:27.900 --> 10:29.090
That's actually my phone.

10:29.090 --> 10:30.800
See, it's only Kayoko's phone.

10:30.800 --> 10:32.460
Here, let's drink up, Abagold.

10:33.120 --> 10:35.240
So it was Mineko's phone.

10:35.240 --> 10:36.310
Aren't you going to answer it?

10:36.310 --> 10:38.270
It would be rude of me to answer the phone with guests over.

10:40.550 --> 10:41.850
Excuse me for one second!

10:43.660 --> 10:45.520
Come on, have some more beer.

10:45.520 --> 10:47.340
Or maybe you'd like some bourbon instead.

10:47.340 --> 10:49.700
Have some more oden, Abasilver.

10:53.250 --> 10:55.730
Where could Master Vamp possibly be?

10:55.730 --> 10:57.920
He's not picking up.

10:58.410 --> 10:58.990
Isn't this song...

11:01.960 --> 11:03.710
Master Vamp!

11:07.720 --> 11:09.110
What's wrong, Red?

11:09.110 --> 11:10.570
What was that all about?

11:10.570 --> 11:13.480
I found a huge rat in the closet.

11:14.030 --> 11:16.720
I swear I'm never going to Hokkaido.

11:17.320 --> 11:18.800
Never!

11:19.200 --> 11:21.310
We want to go to Hokkaido!

11:21.310 --> 11:22.510
Not happening!

11:24.140 --> 11:26.490
That night, Red sent a bill for the window repairs

11:26.490 --> 11:29.900
to Vamp's Rakutin phone.
